120.preflightReason:
The brief has a concrete, verifiable deliverable. It asks for one composition root that:
- registers the daily tick, Mon-Fri 09:30-17:30 IST;
- connects Supabase prospects, GHL (email, with WhatsApp when GHL_WA_PHONE_ID is set and email fallback otherwise), the short-form audit engine and Slack;
- reads templates from agents/outreach-sequencer/templates;
- wires setOutreachReplyDeps so POST /outreach/ghl-reply works;
- stays dry-run until OUTREACH_LIVE=1.

Acceptance is measurable: unit tests render all five touches for a fixture prospect, and a dry-run tick on Railway logs five rendered touches. It also says which base to branch from (main, which already has the PR #104 modules) and what not to recreate. It explains why the earlier attempts (#108, #116) were closed.

It does not violate any SKILL.md §8 Never guardrail. Live sends are gated behind OUTREACH_LIVE=1, so nothing goes to production by default. It installs no external plugins or script tags, and it deletes no content. It does not change pricing or positioning, and it makes no DNS or page-status changes. The work sits in services/ and agents/, which the runner may write on a branch behind the CI gate.

The logs//outreach-sequencer.md proof file is runtime output. The service writes it on Railway, so the PR itself must not add or edit anything under logs/ or decisions/. The implementer should treat the proof as a post-merge runtime artifact and attach it as evidence, not commit it.
